From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Beauchamp <florent.beauchamp@vates.tech>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:38:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: block-vhd: preallocate new blocks with
 FALLOC_FL_ZERO_RANGE

With preallocation (local ext/xfs SRs), allocate_block() writes zeros
over each new block (gap, bitmap and 2 MiB of data) with a synchronous
write(), blocking the event loop: a guest writing 4 KiB into a new block
costs 2 MiB of synchronous I/O, and a block written whole is written
twice.

Use FALLOC_FL_ZERO_RANGE instead: the range reads as zeros whatever it
held before (the old footer, a block of an earlier allocation whose BAT
update failed), for tapdisk and for any other reader of the file, the
space is still reserved, but nothing is written (unwritten extents on
ext4/xfs). Writing zeros remains the fallback when the file system does
not support it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/block-vhd.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block-vhd.c b/drivers/block-vhd.c
index 3d0b5605..f82e7bce 100644
--- a/drivers/block-vhd.c
+++ b/drivers/block-vhd.c
@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@
 #include <sys/mman.h>
 #include <limits.h>
 #include <dlfcn.h>
+#include <linux/falloc.h>
 
 #include "debug.h"
 #include "libvhd.h"
@@ -1697,13 +1698,26 @@ allocate_block(struct vhd_state *s, uint32_t blk)
 	DBG(TLOG_DBG, "blk: 0x%04x, pbwo: 0x%08"PRIx64"\n",
 	    blk, s->bat.pbw_offset);
 
-	if (lseek(s->vhd.fd, offset, SEEK_SET) == (off_t)-1) {
+	size  = vhd_sectors_to_bytes(s->spb + s->bm_secs + gap);
+
+	/*
+	 * The range must read as zeros, whatever it held before (the old
+	 * footer, a block of an earlier allocation whose BAT update failed),
+	 * for any reader of the file: FALLOC_FL_ZERO_RANGE does it without
+	 * writing the data (unwritten extents), and still reserves the space.
+	 * Writing zeros remains the fallback.
+	 */
+	if (!fallocate(s->vhd.fd, FALLOC_FL_ZERO_RANGE, offset, size))
+		count = size;
+	else if (errno != EOPNOTSUPP) {
+		err = -errno;
+		ERR(s, err, "zero range failed (offset %"PRIu64")\n", offset);
+		return err;
+	} else if (lseek(s->vhd.fd, offset, SEEK_SET) == (off_t)-1) {
 		ERR(s, -errno, "lseek failed\n");
 		return -errno;
-	}
-
-	size  = vhd_sectors_to_bytes(s->spb + s->bm_secs + gap);
-	count = write(s->vhd.fd, vhd_zeros(size), size);
+	} else
+		count = write(s->vhd.fd, vhd_zeros(size), size);
 	if (count != size) {
 		err = count < 0 ? -errno : -ENOSPC;
 		ERR(s, -errno,
